      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-45593",
      ":question/problem": "The function $l(x) = 2x + 9$ models the number of subscribers on a travel website while $e(x) = 2^{x}$ models the number of subscribers on a mathematical resources website, where $x$ is the number of weeks since the launch of each site. Assuming that both sites were launched on the same day, after how many weeks will the mathematical resources website have more subscribers than the travel website?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
